    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Current date and time: {{ $now }}\nTimezone: Europe/Zurich.\n\nAnalyze the Telegram message and classify the user's intent.\n\nReturn structured data with exactly these fields:\nintent\ntitle\nstart\nend\nnew_start\nnew_end\nnew_date\nnew_time\nnew_duration_minutes\nuser_message\nchat_id\nlanguage\n\nRules:\n\n1. If the user asks to create, schedule, add, book, or plan a new calendar event:\nintent = create_calendar_event\n\n2. If the user asks what is in the calendar, what events they have, their schedule, appointments, meetings, or plans for a date or period:\nintent = read_calendar\n\n3. If the user asks to move, reschedule, change, rename, or otherwise modify an existing calendar event:\nintent = update_calendar_event\n\n4. Otherwise:\nintent = general_chat\n\nFor create_calendar_event:\n- title = name of the new event\n- start = event start as ISO 8601\n- end = event end as ISO 8601\n- new_start = \"\"\n- new_end = \"\"\n\nFor read_calendar:\n- title = \"\"\n- start = beginning of the requested period as ISO 8601\n- end = end of the requested period as ISO 8601\n- new_start = \"\"\n- new_end = \"\"\n\nFor update_calendar_event:\n- title = title of the existing event\n- start = original event start as ISO 8601\n- end = original event end as ISO 8601\n- new_start = \"\"\n- new_end = \"\"\n- new_date = the new date as YYYY-MM-DD, ONLY if the user names a new day (for example tomorrow, Friday, 25 November); otherwise \"\"\n- new_time = the new start time as HH:mm (24 hours), ONLY if the user names a new time; otherwise \"\"\n- new_duration_minutes = the new duration in minutes, ONLY if the user names a duration; otherwise 0\n- Never fill in a date or time the user did not say. Example: \"move the meeting to 2 pm\" → new_date = \"\", new_time = \"14:00\", new_duration_minutes = 0.\n- If the user only gives a relative shift (for example \"one hour later\"), leave new_date, new_time and new_duration_minutes empty.\n\nFor general_chat:\n- title = \"\"\n- start = \"\"\n- end = \"\"\n- new_start = \"\"\n- new_end = \"\"\n\nFor every intent except update_calendar_event: new_date = \"\", new_time = \"\", new_duration_minutes = 0.\n\nResolve relative dates such as today, tomorrow, next Monday, next week, and in two hours relative to the current date and time above.\n\nUse timezone Europe/Zurich.\n\nIf duration is given, calculate end or new_end accordingly.\n\nAlways copy the user's original Telegram message exactly into user_message.\nDo not summarize, translate, or rewrite user_message.\n\nAlways copy the Telegram chat ID exactly into chat_id.\n\nAlways set language to the ISO 639-1 code of the language of the user's message (for example de, ru, en).\n\nDo not answer the user conversationally. Only classify and extract structured data.\n\nTelegram chat ID:\n{{ $json.message.chat.id }}\n\nUser message:\n{{ $json.message.text }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
